In this example, we use the delta method to calculate the odds ratio, the associated standard errors, and confidence intervals within a logistic regression model.

```{r}
#| message = FALSE
library(package = "betaDelta")
```

```{r}
object <- stats::glm(
  formula = vs ~ wt + disp,
  family = "binomial",
  data = mtcars
)
def <- list("exp(wt)", "exp(disp)")
DeltaGeneric(
  object = object,
  def = def,
  alpha = 0.05
)
```

## Methods

```{r}
delta <- DeltaGeneric(
  object = object,
  def = def,
  alpha = 0.05
)
```

### summary

Summary of the results of `DeltaGeneric()`.

```{r}
summary(object = delta)
```

### coef

Calculate the estimates.

```{r}
stats::coef(object = delta)
```

### vcov

Calculate the sampling covariance matrix.

```{r}
stats::vcov(object = delta)
```

### confint

Generate confidence intervals.

```{r}
stats::confint(object = delta, level = 0.95)
```

